    "final.course_reflection": "This activity gave me a better understanding of how robot motion works and how to develop and test a motion program with an AI assistant. I also learned that even though AI can be helpful when implementing the functions a robot needs, it does not automatically give the correct answer. We still need to review and verify the code before testing and running it because there can be mistakes or test cases that we may not think about. I also learned that technical work needs to consider the environment around the robot. A robot may be able to move from one position to another correctly, but it also needs to be aware of its surroundings and stay within a safe area when operating around people or objects. What stood out to me the most was how important it is to be careful when using AI tools. I should not just trust the output because it looks correct. I need to understand what the code is doing, check it against the requirements, test it, and make changes when needed. This activity showed me that AI can be useful for robotics, but the person using it is still responsible for making sure the final result is correct and safe.\n",
    "final.synthesis": "Even if the robot motion program works correctly, it does not mean it will work well in the real world without any complications. One example would be if the robot has to move to a certain position at a certain time, but there is an object or a person in the way. It would not be safe for the robot to continue its mission without detecting the obstacle. The robot would need sensors to detect people or objects and stop before getting too close to them. Additional evidence would be needed by testing the robot in a real or shared environment and observing how it reacts to obstacles and people. This would help show if the robot is safe and works properly around others.\n",
